WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.020
(lively music)

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.800
- [Jesse] In Gornergrat we
can see almost everything,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.690
galaxies, nebulas;

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.710
the best thing you can
see here is the Milky Way.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.730
It's very bright,

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.680
and you can see a lot of
shooting stars and stuff.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.110
Some nights are so good that
it's one of the best places

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.423
to observe in the world.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.080
- [Narrator] And the best part?

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.960
This view comes with a room.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.223
Up here they take reservations.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.820
Gornergrat is a special place

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.130
that opens up the universe to everyone.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.050
Perched on top of the Swiss Alps

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.600
at over 10,000 feet,

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.420
it's a hotel, restaurant
and an observatory.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.182
What might seem like an unlikely mix

00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:46.023
has turned into one of
Switzerland's most precious places.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.060
- The Kulmhotel Gornergrat
was built in 1907.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.820
Some parts of the building

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.600
are still the same as in the beginning.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.540
We have 22 rooms.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.700
There are four or five days a year

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.620
where there are 5,000 people.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.980
It's the highest hotel in Switzerland

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.070
and the second highest in Europe.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.980
Special thing up here is the
mountain you can see around.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.620
There is Monte Rosa

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.020
and then the Breithorn,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.923
and everybody in the world
knows the Matterhorn.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.750
We serve mostly traditional Swiss food,

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.620
cheese fondue,

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.830
rosti with sausage on it and onion sauce,

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.150
and also the Alpine macaroni.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.540
It's really special for me

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.030
because I love the mountains

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.910
and up here in the night it's very calm

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.573
and the sky is really amazing.

00:01:42.985 --> 00:01:46.318
(classical piano music)

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.680
- These domes are here
from the '60s until now

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.920
but astronomy here in the mountains

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.750
go back to beginning of 1900.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.880
Scientists from all over
the world have been here.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.520
If you want to do astronomy

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.340
you have to have really good conditions,

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.940
and it's a fact that the best conditions

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.843
you have up here in the mountains.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.830
- [Narrator] Lack of light
pollution and dry air

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.290
have meant that people like Jesse

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.363
can really observe space from here.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.320
But even with the naked eye

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.170
anyone can observe the
night beauty at Gornergrat.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.800
- [Jesse] One of the best
places I've been for sure.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.890
You go out on the terrace

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.460
and you see this huge band of the sky,

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.340
and it's just so bright;

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.510
it's amazing.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.890
- [Narrator] And like the stars above,

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.950
Gornergrat shines bright in
the middle of the Swiss Alps,

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.953
keeping the gateway to space
open for many years to come.

00:02:41.043 --> 00:02:43.710
(chiming music)

